# Vauxhall Wyvern, Velox and Cresta E-series saloon, 1951-1957.
#
# The E-series: the Wyvern EIX and the Velox EIP/EIPV on one shell, joined in
# August 1954 by the Cresta E as the trimmed version of the Velox. The
# four-door saloon is modelled; the aftermarket estate conversions are not.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vauxhall_Cresta
#
# Dimensions: Velox 4,369 x 1,702 x 1,613 mm, wheelbase 2,616 mm. The Wyvern
# is 4,382 mm long to 1952 and 4,337 mm after; the Cresta E is 4,400 x 1,690 x
# 1,560. The Velox figures are modelled and the variations are recorded.
#
# Shape reference: image 1 is NOT a true level profile; the flank is
# estimated within the published dimensions.
#
# Colours: grade (d); no period Vauxhall colour list was found. Black, Grey,
# Blue and Green are plain period names. Weights 12, 10, 9, 8, total 39,
# provisional.
#
# Speed 125 km/h. Comfort 40/240, on the line 180 + 1.5 x 40. Classes 1,2.
# Dates: intro October 1951; retires staggered 1967-1970 as a road tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-wyvern-velox-cresta-e.blend.
# Interchange: citycars/4.5/vauxhall-wyvern-velox-cresta-e.dae. References:
# citycars/references/vauxhall-wyvern-velox-cresta-e/ (gitignored).
#
# Accepted deviations: one shared shell on Velox dimensions with late Cresta
# exterior detail. The earlier Wyvern and Velox grille and rear treatments are
# not separate variants.


obj=citycar
name=VauxhallWyvernVeloxCrestaE(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=12
intro_year=1951
intro_month=10
retire_year=1970
retire_month=6
speed=125
class=1,2
